# One thing at a time: the column tells a mixture apart.
# Three colourless liquids dissolved in water look like one liquid.
# The column disagrees: each solute spends its own share of time in
# the stationary phase, set by the same partition coefficient that
# runs the separating funnel, and so each arrives alone.
register lv1
add v1 water 100mL
add v1 methanol 0.05mol
add v1 ethanol 0.1mol
add v1 propanone 0.05mol
chromatograph v1
# The same injection read closer: retention times, widths, areas —
# and K itself, the number doing all the work.
register lv3
chromatograph v1
